ReShiki licensing
=================

Original ReShiki code and documentation are licensed, at your option, under
either the MIT License (LICENSE-MIT) or the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSE-APACHE). The SPDX expression for this choice is:

    MIT OR Apache-2.0

Third-party material is excluded from this dual-license grant. Code, data,
and other material copied, ported, adapted, or bundled from other projects
remain subject to their respective licenses and notices. Translating code
into Rust does not replace those terms. File-specific notices and the
licenses and attribution records in licenses/ and vendor/ take precedence
for that material. See NOTICE for the locations of those records.

Choosing a license for original ReShiki code does not remove obligations
under the licenses of included third-party material. Preserve the applicable
copyright notices, license texts, disclaimers, and attribution records when
redistributing source or binaries.

Optional LGPL component: axtb (xTB calculations)
------------------------------------------------

Builds made with the Cargo feature `xtb`, which include the official macOS
and Linux desktop releases, also contain axtb, an implementation of the xTB
methods, built from the fork at https://github.com/Ameyanagi/axtb at the
revision recorded in Cargo.lock and licenses/axtb/SOURCE. axtb is licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or later
(LGPL-3.0-or-later). It is not covered by the MIT OR Apache-2.0 grant above,
which applies to original ReShiki code only, including the code that calls
axtb. ReShiki builds without that feature, and the Python, npm, crates and
web packages, do not contain axtb.

licenses/axtb/ holds the GNU license texts, axtb's own notice and the pinned
revision. Each release that contains axtb publishes the complete
corresponding source and the steps to rebuild ReShiki with a modified axtb;
see docs/xtb-licensing.md.

(This section is pending outside review before the first release that
includes xTB.)
